## Writing standards

TARGET: 4,300–4,900 words per chapter (see CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md for per-chapter target)
POV: Close third person, Aaron Mercer throughout. No POV shifts.
TENSE: Past tense throughout.

Aaron's voice (NON-NEGOTIABLE, evolved from Book 1):
- Precise, dry, calibrated — now carrying three-plus years of institutional weight
- Technical vocabulary for emotion: "elevated threat-response indexing" not "I was afraid"
- Dry humor is structural — he builds the setup, the weight lands quietly at the end
- New in Book 2: he now sometimes withholds information deliberately, as practice, not reflex — this should read as costing him more, not less, than it did the first time

Station/facility atmosphere requirements (at least ONE per chapter):
- Specific detail of the physical environment (Geneva facility, not Helix Perimeter — permanent secure building, not station architecture)
- Scientific/institutional work specificity: what the Conduit interface does, what sessions show, what the logs say

